ink of anything okay so we know that  zahra will be moving 5 units to the  right and 4 units upwards we know that  for sure no matter which shortest path  she takes it will be total of 9 units  out of which 5 will be to the right and  4 will be upwards so we write our five  times and you four times this is what we  need to arrange all possible  arrangements of these nine letters will  give us the number of different shortest  paths Sara can take this should remind  you of the anagram problem we had solved  we had the word excessive as there were  nine letters we wrote 9 factorial e was  present thrice hence divided this by 3  factorial s was present twice hence  divided again by 2 factorial we applied  the same logic here as there are nine  letters present we write nine factorial  R appears five times so divide this by 5  factorial and as u appears four times we  divide this by 4 factorial this also  gives us the same answer all three give  us the answer as 126 zahra can take 126  different shortest paths to reach the  gate shop you may use any method you  like depends on what you are comfortable  with but make sure you understand the
 

